<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Monck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1608">1608</a>–<a href="/years/1670">1670</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as George Monck, 1st Duke of Albemarle, George Monk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Monck was an English soldier who fought for the king and then for Parliament and was Cromwell's commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> in the 1650s. After the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> he marched his army from Scotland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1660, restored the excluded members of Parliament and arranged the return of Charles II. He was rewarded with the title Duke of Albemarle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-monck.jpg" alt="George Monck" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Peter Lely · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Monck_1st_Duke_of_Albemarle_Studio_of_Lely.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
